      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I'll write the improved test. The original only tests one case and has unused imports. I'll clean up the imports, add a display name, and add representative cases covering each distinct version-string format (old `1.x` style, single-integer style, and the Android `0.9` variant).The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored test removes unused imports, adds a `@DisplayName` annotation and Javadoc explaining the three distinct version-string formats, and extends coverage to representative cases from each format (`\"0.9\"`, classic `\"1.x\"`, and modern single-integer `\"N\"`), while preserving identical runtime behaviour."
